<title>POLAND: BRE surges on Commerzbank news.</title>
<headline>BRE surges on Commerzbank news.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish Bank Rozwoju Eksportu SA (BRE) surged 9.9 percent to 89 zlotys on the news that Germany's Commerzbank AG might increase its stake in the bank to over 50 percent, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;The Commerzbank news and expectations that a public tender offer will be called made the stock rise,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Analysts said BRE might extend its gains in the next few sessions. @</p>
<p>On Tuesday the Polish Securities Commission cleared Commerzbank to raise its stake in BRE beyond 33 percent and said it would not object to Commerzbank gaining more than 50 percent of BRE shares if it resulted from a purchase of shares through a public tender offer. -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
